# Project Standards

- Use the `app/` package layout: routes in `app/api/`, config in `app/core/`, DB in `app/db/`
- Name Pydantic models in `app/schemas/`, not `pydanticValidators/`
- Keep routes thin — delegate business logic to `app/services/` when adding domain code
- Use type hints on all function signatures
- Prefer async endpoints and `AsyncSession` for database access
- Return standard FastAPI/Pydantic responses — no custom `{status_code, message, data}` envelopes
- Import settings from `app.core.config`, never read `os.environ` directly in routes
